### Tier 4: Scheduler Architecture Changes

With instant spawning, your scheduler bottleneck shifts:

```go
// Old model: Bin-packing focused (containers are expensive to move)
// New model: Request-routing focused (spawn anywhere instantly)

type InstantSpawnScheduler struct {
    // No longer tracking "where containers are"
    // Instead: "where SHOULD this request go"

    routingTable   *ConsistentHash  // For stateful affinity
    capacityMap    *RealtimeCapacity
    latencyMap     *LatencyOracle   // Network latency between nodes
}

func (s *InstantSpawnScheduler) Schedule(req Request) Node {
    // With instant spawn, optimize for:
    // 1. Network latency to user
    // 2. Data locality (if stateful)
    // 3. Cost (spot instances, etc.)

    // NOT for: "which node has a running container"
    // Because we can spawn anywhere in <100ms

    candidates := s.capacityMap.NodesWithCapacity(req.Resources)

    if req.HasStateAffinity() {
        return s.routingTable.GetNode(req.AffinityKey)
    }

    // Pure latency optimization
    return s.latencyMap.ClosestTo(req.ClientRegion, candidates)
}
```

